  "editorial_note": "GitHub listed thirteen projects this Wednesday morning, and eight of them were already in recent digests with no material change, so today's edition is short. Floci is the most broadly useful newcomer: ==a free, MIT-licensed local AWS emulator== aimed squarely at former LocalStack Community users. Hex brings push-to-talk dictation with on-device models and an agent-friendly command line; Spotify's Portal plugins show how a company can hand its service catalog to coding agents; and ai-goofish-monitor turns a vision model into a second-hand shopping filter, with clear terms-of-service caveats. Curation order reflects practical interest, not GitHub rank. Trending is not a release date or an endorsement.",
  "coverage_notes": [
    "All 13 listing entries were inspected. Exact primary public GitHub repository metadata and recent releases were checked for all 13 at about 07:01 UTC, with README files for the four picks; all 13 were active and unarchived. All four picks have an explicit licence (MIT or Apache-2.0) confirmed in their LICENSE files.",
    "No repeats today. Eight entries featured before were left out without a material change: vercel-labs/agent-desktop, max-sixty/worktrunk, JustVugg/colibri and D4Vinci/Scrapling (3 November; no new releases since), thedotmack/claude-mem (2 November; latest release v15.9.0 was already noted yesterday), mattpocock/skills (31 October), Donchitos/Claude-Code-Game-Studios (30 October; no commits since 19 October) and shiyu-coder/Kronos (20 October; no commits since April).",
    "Not picked: p-e-w/heretic, whose default configuration removes language models' safety refusals; left out again as an editorial choice, as with earlier jailbreak tooling.",
    "anomalyco/hex was on the 2 November list and passed over then because it overlapped Handy; it is picked today for the agent features and the v3.3.0 changes described on its card.",
    "No security-focused project was on today's list.",
    "The preceding seven calendar dates, 28 October-3 November, were checked for local history; all seven editions exist.",
    "The official listing was captured at 08:00:42 Europe/Paris. Literal stars-today labels are GitHub's displayed period figures; API total stars and README evidence were checked separately at the times shown per card. They are not an independently audited rolling 24-hour growth measurement.",
    "Feature, privacy, speed and savings descriptions are the maintainers' own, including Floci's startup and memory comparison, Hex's on-device claim and shunt's token savings. No candidate code, installer, plugin or model was installed, downloaded or run, and none of this is a security audit or endorsement."
  ],
  "projects": [
    {
      "repository": "floci-io/floci",
      "url": "https://github.com/floci-io/floci",
      "trending_rank": 8,
      "description": "A ==free local emulator of AWS services== for development, tests and CI. You point the AWS CLI, an SDK, Terraform, CDK or OpenTofu at localhost:4566 and work against S3, DynamoDB, SQS, Lambda, IAM and well over a hundred other service names without a cloud account or auth token. Lambda, RDS, ECS, EKS, OpenSearch and a few others run in real Docker containers rather than shallow mocks, and a browser console shows the local resources.",
      "why_interesting": "First time on our list. The README presents it as ==a drop-in replacement for LocalStack Community==, which it says now needs an auth token: the same port, translated LocalStack environment variables, unchanged init scripts and a Testcontainers-compatible ready line. It is MIT-licensed, ships a Docker image and a standalone binary, and releases often; 2.4.0 (31 October) added many API Gateway and Auto Scaling operations.",
      "caveat": "An emulator is not AWS: ==behaviour and permissions can differ from the real service==, so check the per-operation coverage page and keep tests against real AWS for anything that matters. By default any credentials are accepted, and the console and container-backed services ==need the Docker socket, which gives the emulator control of your Docker host==. The startup, memory and image-size comparisons are the maintainers' own figures. The project dates from February 2026. We did not run it.",
      "category": "Developer tools / cloud testing",
      "language": "Java",
      "license": "MIT",
      "stars_total": 29055,
      "stars_period": 482,
      "stars_period_label": "482 stars today",
