    {
      "repository": "spotify/portal-ai-plugins",
      "url": "https://github.com/spotify/portal-ai-plugins",
      "trending_rank": 7,
      "description": "Spotify's official ==plugins that bring its Spotify Portal developer platform into coding agents== (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor and pi). They wrap the Portal CLI in eleven workflows: search the software catalog and documentation in plain language, write a short briefing on a service's owners, health and incidents, run Portal actions with dry-run and confirmation steps, and create, run and check Fleetshift fleet-wide code changes that open pull requests.",
      "why_interesting": "First time on our list. It is a worked example of ==giving agents an organisation's service catalog as context== instead of letting them guess who owns what, and the actions workflow builds in previews and confirmations before anything changes. A second plugin, shunt, sends bulk file reads and boilerplate to cheaper models through Portal's AiKA assistant; the maintainers claim 82-94% token savings, which we did not verify.",
      "caveat": "It is only useful if your organisation ==pays for Spotify Portal==, a commercial product sold through its sales team and AWS Marketplace. Shunt ==installs hooks that stop Claude reading large files== and sends that content to your Portal instance instead, so check what your company allows. The repository has no releases, its last commit was 23 October, and the setup runs the Portal CLI from npm. Apache-2.0. We did not install it.",
      "category": "AI agents / internal developer platforms",
      "language": "TypeScript",
      "license": "Apache-2.0",
      "stars_total": 3099,
