    {
      "repository": "Usagi-org/ai-goofish-monitor",
      "url": "https://github.com/Usagi-org/ai-goofish-monitor",
      "trending_rank": 9,
      "description": "A self-hosted ==monitor for Xianyu (Goofish), Alibaba's second-hand marketplace==, with a web dashboard. You create watch tasks with keywords, price ranges, region and posting-time filters, either by hand or by describing what you want in plain language; a Playwright browser searches on a schedule, a vision-capable AI model judges each new listing from its text and photos, and matches are pushed to ntfy, Bark, Telegram, WeChat Work or a webhook.",
      "why_interesting": "First time on our list. It is a complete, practical example of ==an AI model used as a shopping filter==: the model writes the judging criteria from your request, then scores listings against them, and the results, price history and logs live in SQLite behind a FastAPI web interface. It runs in one Docker container with Chromium included, and there is an English README.",
      "caveat": "It logs in with ==your Xianyu session cookies, exported through a third-party Chrome extension==, and rotates accounts and proxies when the site's risk controls trigger. The README itself asks users to respect Xianyu's terms and avoid frequent requests, and accounts can be restricted. Every listing's photos go to the AI provider you configure, at your cost. The web login ==defaults to admin/admin123==, and v2.5 (9 October) fixed a path-traversal bug. No commits since 10 October. We did not run it.",
      "category": "AI automation / marketplace monitoring",
      "language": "Python",
      "license": "MIT",
